AB  - Background: Penile cancer is a rare malignancy with an incidence of 0.6-2.1 per 100,000. Squamous cell carcinoma (SqCC) is the most common penile malignancy. PD-L1 co-stimulates PD-1 to suppress T-cell-mediated antitumor immunity. Methods: Retrospective cohort study of 76 male patients with penile SqCC; PD-L1 levels were measured on biopsy slides and correlated with tumor stage. Results: PD-L1 positivity was identified in 25/76 patients. Significant correlation between PD-L1 expression and metastasis (p=0.022); no significant correlation with N stage (p=0.167). Conclusions: PD-L1 is highly expressed in advanced-stage penile SqCC (32.9%), associated with high-risk clinicopathologic features and poor outcomes, suggesting potential for immunotherapy in advanced disease.
