AB  - SPP1 was identified as the most differentially up-regulated gene in penile cancer tissues and positive lymph node tissues via whole transcriptome sequencing of 8 paired specimens. TCGA/TIMER analysis showed SPP1 was significantly associated with B cells, CD8+ T cells, CD4+ T cells, macrophages, neutrophils and dendritic cells. Survival analysis of 183 PSCC paraffin sections showed low-SPP1 patients had significantly better survival than high-SPP1 patients. ssGSEA/CIBERSORT analysis linked SPP1 to immune infiltration; GSVA/GSEA linked SPP1 to MAPK, mTOR, Wnt and immune checkpoint (PD-1/PD-L1) pathways. SPP1 may be an effective biomarker for predicting prognosis and immunotherapy efficacy in PSCC.
