AB  - Locally advanced penile squamous cell carcinoma (PSCC) with unresectable inguinal lymph nodes carries a poor prognosis and limited benefit from surgery alone. We report a locally advanced PSCC patient with bulky, fixed inguinal lymph node metastasis and genital skin ulcers who completed inguinal lymph node dissection and achieved pathologically complete response after conversion therapy with immunotherapy (tislelizumab) plus chemotherapy. Conclusion: for unresectable locally advanced PSCC, neoadjuvant immunotherapy combined with chemotherapy is a potential conversion treatment approach; biomarkers of immune efficacy require further study, and clinical trials are needed.
